lane stops at the verdict gate** until `docs/reviews/WI-<n>-REVIEW-A.md`\n  is hand-compiled (rounds time-ordered, governing line last). Compile it on the\n  lane as a record commit (docs/reviews/ never stales the APPROVE), then run\n  `integrate.py --root . integrate` FROM THE TRUNK ROOT.\n- **Refresh misfire:** a lane cut BEFORE a trunk commit that moved\n  `docs/archive/last_approved/` cannot refresh — `integrate.refresh` does\n  `merge --no-commit` + `add -A`, so trunk's snapshot delta is STAGED and the\n  staged mirror rule + approval-fresh both red. Remedy (precedent 9bdd56b6):\n  merge trunk into the lane as a plain commit first; it costs a round (a\n  non-record commit after the APPROVE).\n- **Adjudication lanes (brief=disposition) loop (C6):** the ADJUDICATE session may\n  put `## Dispositions` in the verdict file (must be in the SPEC); a refused\n  close makes the dispatcher resume the lane as fresh ADJUDICATE sessions\n  forever. Stop the loop (`pkill -f 'agent_loop.py --root'`), rework the spec,\n  then close via `handback.close_adjudication(root, branch)` from python at the\n  trunk root, draw a verification round, compile the rollup, integrate.\n- **Hostile Opus rounds** (general-purpose subagent, writes\n  `NNN-REVIEW-A-<sha7>-supervisor.md`, no commits) found real defects every time,\n  including in MY OWN owner brief (claimed external.toml unaffected; proposed a\n  byte-level snapshot RESTORE that the mirror invariant forbids). Never\n  rubber-stamp; keep the same reviewer agent for verification rounds.\n- **Record-only rework is cheap:** docs/reviews + docs/log.d never stale the\n  verdict; docs/work and docs/archive/work DO.\n- The classifier blocks scripts that rewrite docs/log.md on trunk and even\n  `git show <held-branch>:docs/log.md`; ask the owner rather than work around.\n- Opus subagents can hit a session rate limit (429) mid-task; do small edits\n  yourself with Read+Edit.\n\nSee [[supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons]], [[codex-effort